# TB323FU initramfs layout, annotated (gen_init_cpio format).
# build.sh generates the real list with absolute paths; this file documents
# what goes in and why. "ours" = source in this repository.
#
# /bin/busybox            third-party: static aarch64 BusyBox (tested 1.36.1)
# /init                   ours: kernel/initramfs/init (MIT)
# /bin/back-to-android    ours: android/back-to-android (MIT)
# /bin/keyhold            ours: userspace/platform/src/keyhold.c, built static
#                         (the volume up+down chord)
# /bin/gpu-probe          ours: kernel/initramfs/gpu-probe.c (GPL-2.0), optional,
#                         static; one line about the Adreno in the summary
# /etc/android-boot.sha256  per device, optional: hash of YOUR Android boot
#                         image (never commit it). Without it init reads the
#                         root's /etc/tb323fu/android-boot.sha256
# /etc/usb-shell          only with build.sh -u (development images): empty
#                         marker; init then starts a root shell without
#                         password on ttyGS0 and telnet on usb0
# /dev/console            char 5:1 -- without it init has no stdin/stdout
# /font.psf               third-party: console-setup Lat15-Terminus28x14
#                         (readable on 1904x3040; the kernel's fonts are small)
# /proc /sys /sys/fs/pstore  mount points
#
# /lib/modules/<release>.sqfs  with build.sh -m (shared modules): ALL modules of
#                         this kernel (make modules_install INSTALL_MOD_STRIP=1,
#                         aw882xx in extra/, depmod output), squashfs xz. init
#                         mounts it on /lib/modules/<release> (dir in the image),
#                         loads the early modules below from it by modules.dep,
#                         and moves the mount into the chosen root before
#                         switch_root. The roots carry no modules of their own.
# /lib/modules/*.ko       without -m: only the early modules, flat, from the
#                         kernel build, debug info stripped. Modules on
#                         purpose, loaded by init after the USB shell is up:
#   qcom_pil_info qcom_common qcom_sysmon qcom_q6v5 qcom_q6v5_pas
#                         remoteproc PAS: attaches to the charger firmware
#                         (SoCCP) the bootloader already runs -> pmic-glink
#                         (battery, Type-C); a bad attach still leaves a way in
#   nt36536_ts            touch; downloads its firmware to the IC's SRAM
#
# /lib/firmware/...       vendor firmware, from YOUR device (firmware/), never
#                         committed; only with build.sh -f (release images
#                         have none). Wanted here because these drivers
#                         probe before a root is mounted:
#   qcom/gen80200_{sqe.fw,gmu.bin,aqe.fw}, qcom/kaanapali/Lenovo/baldur/gen80200_zap.mbn
#                         Adreno 840 (the fbdev console opens the DRM device)
#   novatek/novatek_ts_fw.bin            touch
#   qca/brhbtnv20.bin qca/brhbtfw20.mbn (qca/brhbtfw20.tlv optional)  Bluetooth
#   ath12k/WCN7860/hw2.0/{amss.bin,m3.bin,aux_ucode.bin,board.bin,regdb.bin,qdss.cfg}
#                         Wi-Fi (names ath12k asks for; see firmware/manifest.tsv)
#   regulatory.db regulatory.db.p7s      third-party: wireless-regdb (cfg80211
#                         is built in and reads it at boot)
